WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:13.850
Discovered by Karl Wilhelm Feuerbach in eighteen twenty-two, X eleven is the Feuerbach Point: the celebrated point where the incircle centered at X one and the nine-point circle centered at X five kiss in internal tangency.

2
00:00:14.270 --> 00:00:25.660
Its trilinear coordinates are one minus cosine of B minus C, to one minus cosine of C minus A, to one minus cosine of A minus B, with algebraic barycentrics s minus a times b minus c squared.

3
00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:35.440
Because the point of tangency of two circles always lies on their line of centers, X eleven lies directly on the Feuerbach line through X one, X five, and X twelve.

4
00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:47.940
X eleven is the harmonic conjugate of X twelve with respect to X one and X five, the isogonal conjugate of X fifty-nine, and lies on the circumcircle of the intouch triangle and the pedal circle of the Spieker center.
